{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 18, "model_name": "mistralai/mixtral-8x7b-instruct-v0.1", "content": " Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the son of Bohemond II of Antioch and Alice of Jerusalem he was born in 1140 and died in 1187 Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a count of Tripoli from 1152 until his death He was also the prince of Galilee and Tiberias from 1174 to 1187 Raymond III Count of Tripoli was the son of Bohemond II of Antioch and Alice of Jerusalem He was born in 1140 and died in 1187\n\nEarly life\n\nRaymond III Count of Tripoli was born in 1140 in Apulia Italy He was the only son of Bohemond II of Antioch and Alice of Jerusalem Raymond III Count of Tripoli spent most of his youth in Apulia and was educated by Peter the Venetian a monk and scholar from the monastery of St. Sabas in Rome Raymond III Count of Tripoli was fluent in Greek and Latin and had a deep understanding of classical literature and philosophy\n\nCount of Tripoli\n\nIn 1152 Raymond III Count of Tripoli succeeded his father as the count of Tripoli He was only 12 years old at the time and was placed under the regency of his mother Hodierna of Jerusalem Raymond III Count of Tripoli's reign was marked by conflicts with the Muslim states surrounding Tripoli and with the Byzantine Empire Raymond III Count of Tripoli also had to deal with the internal struggles of the Crusader states in the Levant\n\nPrince of Galilee and Tiberias\n\nIn 1174 Raymond III Count of Tripoli became the prince of Galilee and Tiberias after the death of his cousin Baldwin III of Jerusalem Raymond III Count of Tripoli's reign as prince was marked by his efforts to strengthen the defenses of the Crusader states in the Levant and to improve relations with the Muslim states in the region Raymond III Count of Tripoli also had to deal with the internal struggles of the Crusader states in the Levant\n\nBattle of Hattin\n\nIn 1187 Raymond III Count of Tripoli participated in the Battle of Hattin against the Muslim leader Saladin Raymond III Count of Tripoli was one of the few Crusader leaders to escape the battle alive but his defeat marked the beginning of the end of the Crusader presence in the Levant Raymond III Count of Tripoli died in 1187\n\nHighlighted section part 1: Early life\nHighlighted section part 2: Count of Tripoli\nHighlighted section part 3: Prince of Galilee and Tiberias", "logprobs": [{"token": "Raymond", "logprob": -9.107174992095679e-05}, {"token": "III", "logprob": -0.0001829695247579366}, {"token": "Count", "logprob": -0.5162993669509888}, {"token": "of", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "Tri", "logprob": -6.198863957251888e-06}, {"token": "pol", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "i", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "was", "logprob": -0.15124556422233582}, {"token": "the", "logprob": -2.612416982650757}, {"token": "son", "logprob": -1.9241737127304077}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "Bo", "logprob": -0.00041976699139922857}, {"token": "hem", "logprob": -1.9073468138230965e-06}, {"token": "ond", "logprob": -0.018149960786104202}, {"token": "II", "logprob": -0.0017037175130099058}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -0.7510477900505066}, {"token": "Ant", "logprob": -2.407998726994265e-05}, {"token": "io", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "ch", "logprob": -4.768370445162873e-07}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.1920928244535389e-07}, {"token": "Alice", "logprob": -0.001914812484756112}, {"token": "of", "logprob": -0.001974539365619421}, {"token": "Jerusalem", "logprob": -0.0047534797340631485}, {"token": "he", "logprob": -0.6382312774658203}, {"token": "was", "logprob": -0.0013296105898916721}, {"token": "born", "logprob": -0.0017849955474957824}, {"token": "in", "logprob": -0.08894545584917068}, {"token": "", "logprob": -2.264974000354414e-06}, {"token": "1", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "1", "logprob": -1.5497195136049413e-06}, {"token": "4", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "0", "logprob": -1.19209282445353